WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:04.000
That is who we are!

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:05.440
The Spirit, Anima
Asahina Samidare

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:05.520
The Lizard Knight
Amamiya Yuuhi
Neu Crescent

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.430
The Beast Knights!

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:06.690
The Crow Knight
 Shinonome Mikazuki
 Mu

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:06.690
The Snake Knight
 Hakudou Yayoi
 Sia Moon

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:08.630
Take those who long for our destruction,

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:07.980
The Horse Knight
 Nagumo Souichirou
 Dance Dark

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:08.980
The Black Cat Knight
 Shimaki Hyou
 Kuh Ritter

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:08.980
The Rooster Knight
 Hoshikawa Subaru
 Ly Soleil

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:08.980
The Turtle Knight
 Tsukishiro Yukimachi
 Long Yue

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:10.030
crush them in our jaws,

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.030
The Mouse Knight
 Kusakabe Tarou
 Lance Lumiere

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:10.030
The Owl Knight
 Akane Taiyou
 Loki Helios

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:10.030
The Mantis Knight
 Sorano Hanako
 Kir Sonne

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:11.710
and devour them whole!

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:12.950
Yeah!

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:17.280
<i>To protect the Earth from 
the planet-destroying weapon,</i>

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.920
<i>the Biscuit Hammer...</i>

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.250
The Mage
Animus

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:22.240
<i>To defeat the mage, Animus,</i>

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.360
<i>and...</i>

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:26.330
<i>To fulfill our own ambitions,</i>

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:34.620
<i>the ten surviving Beast Knights 
were united under Anima in late July.</i>

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:39.930
<i>Everyone was crying</i>

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:43.390
<i>Like a star burning blue</i>

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:46.770
<i>Where will we go? What will we see?</i>

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:51.570
<i>We're all going to change, though.</i>

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:08.990
<i>I don't need it, don't want it.</i>

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:11.100
<i>I've already given up on it</i>

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.760
<i>After so many sad farewells</i>

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:15.140
<i>And "take cares"</i>

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:20.460
<i>I want to like the present more than the past, 
the future more than the present.</i>

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:24.550
<i>Gradually my values have changed</i>

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:28.020
<i>I felt more grown up the more they wore away</i>

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:33.910
<i>Lies and betrayals 
are practically civilities</i>

00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:37.410
<i>Everyone ages</i>

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:40.890
<i>But what about the star burning blue?</i>

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:44.230
<i>Our likes and dislikes</i>

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:47.830
<i>They'll all change at some point</i>

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:50.700
<i>A worn-out savior</i>

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:52.380
<i>A medal in a dirty ditch</i>

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:56.210
<i>I don't want to overlook 
their faint glimmers of light</i>

00:01:56.210 --> 00:02:00.010
<i>I hear the sound still ringing from them</i>

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:05.530
<i>Let's move on a bit</i>

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:08.690
You're on!

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:11.980
I, Radical Merry, shall break you!

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:14.690
Strongest

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.690
Magical Marie, prepare yourself!

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:15.570
Hah!

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:18.260
Oh, a new character.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:20.660
<b>Episode 8: Amamiya Yuuhi and the Beast Knights (Part 2)</b>

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:19.990
Crazy outfit.

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:24.480
This contains episodes 27 through 39.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.700
Thanks for letting me borrow it.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:31.170
I'm surprised to learn you watch 
this kind of stuff, though.

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:33.590
I love anime and manga.

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:35.220
Yako's in deep.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.500
She's a cosplayer.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:37.510
Sia!

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:39.450
What's that?

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.720
Someone who wears costumes.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:43.160
Costumes?!

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.890
All right, well, I should be going now.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.060
Cosplay...

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:02.090
What's all this for?

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:04.160
You're not going to show them to anyone.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.620
It's fine.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.300
Nice shot, nice shot.

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:11.630
You should, at least, show them to Amami.

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:13.280
Why Amamiya-kun?

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:14.820
Why him?

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:16.360
Well, whatever.

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:19.670
He'd just think I'm weird.

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:21.750
Now you're just waffling.

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:25.140
What happened to the courage 
you had when we first met?

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:28.370
When we first met, huh?

00:03:38.630 --> 00:03:39.650
Hmm?

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:53.060
U-Um! H-Hold on!

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:55.800
I won't bite! Listen to me!

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:58.550
So snakes are able to talk now?

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:00.650
Ah, she's still asleep!

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:01.510
Wake up!

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:03.730
Wake up, I said!

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:07.900
So what did you want to discuss?

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:08.760
Right.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.810
I want your power to help 
defeat the mage, Animus,

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:15.160
who's plotting to destroy the planet.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:16.860
Okay. Sure.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:19.090
Huh? Were you listening to me?

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:20.930
I'll be saving the planet, right?

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:24.920
I'm not joking when I say it's 
a kill or be killed battle.

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:26.320
I'll do my best.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:30.090
Well, whatever.

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:32.870
In that case, let me explain things.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:36.150
So there you have it.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:39.560
And as an advance reward 
for forging the knight's pact,

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:42.520
I can grant you one wish.

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:44.450
Got it?

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.170
Yeah, mostly.

00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:47.800
So can I do it now?

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:48.760
Do what?

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:50.600
Make my wish.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.990
It's the reward for putting 
your life on the line.

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:55.060
You should give it some more thought.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:58.460
If my life is on the line, 
then isn't it better to do it sooner?

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:01.650
Do you mean you're prepared 
to die at any time?

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:03.160
Yes.

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:07.110
After all, everything that lives 
is guaranteed to die.

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:12.660
My wish is for Mom, Dad, 
and the rest of my family

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:17.120
to die with a smile 
when it's their time to go.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:18.280
Can you do that?

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:19.680
I can.

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:22.360
Whether it's long after 
you've saved the Earth,

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:24.410
or if the end were to 
suddenly come tomorrow,

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:26.800
your family will be able 
to die with a smile.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.410
Thank goodness.

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:30.280
People are guaranteed to die.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:33.050
That's why I make the most of life, 
so I can die without regrets.

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:37.120
Dying with a smile is the 
greatest luxury in this world.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:38.520
So that's my wish.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:40.020
Though, I'm cheating a bit.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.740
You are.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:44.160
Either way, now the pact is forged.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:46.610
I'm Sia Moon.

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:48.570
Hakudou Yayoi.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:51.590
Together we are the Snake Knight.

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:57.360
So I thought I had appeared 
before one crazy woman.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:58.750
Oh, is that so?

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:01.990
You should bring some of that 
fearless attitude with you

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:03.960
when you're interacting with Amami.

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:14.210
Ah.

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:15.080
Nagumo.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:18.480
Good morning.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:22.230
Are you not working today, Nagumo-san?

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:26.530
Uh, Nagumo-dono is unemployed, apparently.

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:28.010
Huh? For real?

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:30.540
Did you two just finish 
your morning training?

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:31.460
Yes.

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:33.950
Then let's go grab breakfast together.

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:36.340
My treat, of course.

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:41.190
You're unemployed, and you have money?

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:43.100
Is he living off his parents?

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:45.340
Wait, given his age...

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:55.270
Sorry.

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:57.280
Hello.

00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:58.520
Oh, Mom?

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:03.200
Hmm? Yeah. I'm doing well.

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:05.340
Work?

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:07.440
Don't worry, it's going well.

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:09.200
Later.

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:12.990
W-Was that from your mother?

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:15.450
It was my wife, we live apart.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:17.570
Wife?!

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:20.910
Y-You call your own wife "Mom"? Then...

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:23.380
Yeah, I have one son.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:25.150
<i>Unemployed with both wife and child?</i>

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:28.090
<i>And he's lying to his wife about his job...</i>

00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:29.540
Um...

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:30.590
What?

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:33.430
How did you and your wife meet?

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:34.460
Hm?

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:37.200
It was back before I became 
a detective, I suppose.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:38.100
A detective?

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.240
Yeah.

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:42.810
Back when I was still on police box 
duty, I got a call about a burglary.

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:48.690
So you seized your wife's heart 
along with the criminal?

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:51.280
<i>She looks so proud of that pun.</i>

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:55.250
May I ask why you quit?

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:02.210
I quit only very recently.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:07.380
Nagumo-san, why are you sleeping here again?

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:10.520
Hm? Oh, Hiwatari, huh?

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:11.670
I'm getting up now.

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:19.840
What's that look for?

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:23.100
Don't shout, you'll embarrass yourself.

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:26.900
Other humans are unable to see and hear me.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:31.060
Oh, I think I'm still waking up.

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:33.870
Are you okay?

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:34.870
Yeah.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.410
Continue to act normal and listen.

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:44.080
Right now, Earth is in danger.

00:08:47.090 --> 00:08:49.500
Thanks for your hard work, Nagumo-san.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:50.860
Yeah.

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:53.720
That serial slasher we've been 
chasing acts way too boldly,

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:55.570
so we've had our hands full.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:58.500
He hasn't given us any leads, has he?

00:08:58.500 --> 00:08:59.560
No.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:02.540
Though the chief got a tip 
that the culprit is going to act

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:05.070
at the place we're heading to now.

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:07.690
Where'd he get a tip like that?

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:08.750
I know.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:11.110
It's probably fake, but we still have to go.

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:12.070
Wha?!

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:17.150
What's the matter?

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:19.070
I-It's nothing.

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:22.640
Looks like this is the place.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:24.880
It's an ordinary neighborhood.

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:26.830
He's really going to strike here?

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:28.310
I don't know.

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:32.010
But it would be dangerous 
to assume he won't.

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:32.840
True.

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:37.960
I can't bear to see an innocent 
child like them get hurt.

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:41.940
Any adult that makes a kid cry is my enemy.

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:45.250
Let's split up and search the area.

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:46.270
Yes!

00:09:46.990 --> 00:09:48.100
Hiwatari.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:53.030
We're law enforcers, not heroes of justice.

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:54.630
Don't forget that.

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:55.940
Yes!

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:01.370
You were saying something 
about Earth being in danger?

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:06.230
Perhaps you should be focused 
on the present danger for now?

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:09.180
Not something I need to hear from you.

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:14.360
We're law enforcers, 
not heroes of justice, huh?

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:19.760
It looks like you take pride 
in being a detective.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:22.750
Hmph. It's nothing like that.

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:26.700
I'm just trying to fulfill my duty.

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:30.230
"Justice" isn't a word you can 
go casually throwing around.

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:31.950
Hmm.

00:10:31.950 --> 00:10:34.720
Sounds like you have 
strong feelings on justice.

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:35.620
Hmph.

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:41.740
Out of my way! Or I'll stab you!

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:42.840
Move it!

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:50.080
Traffic
Safety

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:52.250
Are you all right?

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:54.010
Yes.

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:56.420
The wound isn't that deep.

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:58.130
I see.

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:00.840
Huh?

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:08.850
Hey, that's the chief beside him, isn't it?

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:11.160
You don't think he's the chief's...?

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:12.270
I'll go.

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:19.190
I failed to kill him thanks to some woman.

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:23.510
Even I wouldn't be able to 
make murder go away.

00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:25.660
Your son?

00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:29.470
So that's why you had such 
accurate information on him.

00:11:29.470 --> 00:11:30.980
You, huh?

00:11:30.980 --> 00:11:33.830
Why didn't you stop him if you knew?

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:36.120
He wouldn't listen when I told him.

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:39.670
That's why I sent you two there.

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:42.530
I don't know how to hold back,

00:11:42.530 --> 00:11:44.790
so next time I hope you stop me before I kill—

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:51.180
I'm willing to overlook that one.

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:55.860
Though you do know what will happen 
if you pursue this matter too deeply, right?

00:11:56.920 --> 00:12:03.890
Well, I'm counting on you to continue 
upholding justice and defending the peace.

00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:05.010
Chief.

00:12:06.110 --> 00:12:06.980
Hmph!

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:15.730
Enforcing the law is a tough job, huh?

00:12:15.730 --> 00:12:16.840
Hmph.

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:18.770
By the way, Earth is—

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:22.470
Souji?

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:24.090
<i>Hello, Dad?</i>

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:27.900
<i>I got the birthday present. Thank you!</i>

00:12:27.900 --> 00:12:30.380
<i>Though, about this DVD...</i>

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:32.400
<i>What's </i>Parrotman<i>?</i>

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:35.410
It's an old hero show 
that recently got remastered.

00:12:35.410 --> 00:12:36.980
Back when I was young,

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:40.070
they actually asked me to get 
in costume and appear in it once.

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:41.570
<i>Wow.</i>

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:43.140
I played a villain, though.

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:45.880
<i>Even though you're a cop?</i>

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:48.380
It's a good series. You should watch it.

00:12:48.380 --> 00:12:49.570
<i>Sure.</i>

00:12:49.570 --> 00:12:53.580
<i>Keep up the good work being 
a real hero of justice, Dad.</i>

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:55.340
Yeah. See you later.

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:56.340
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:12:57.420 --> 00:13:01.860
Our enemy is true evil that's trying 
to physically destroy the planet.

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:06.020
You can become one—a real hero of justice.

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:08.190
I'll never be one.

00:13:08.190 --> 00:13:11.210
If our survival is on the line, 
then we'll have to use any means necessary.

00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:13.770
You can't call that a hero of justice.

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:15.900
But very well.

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:17.850
I'm willing to get my hands dirty.

00:13:18.460 --> 00:13:20.180
You believe me?

00:13:20.180 --> 00:13:22.590
I'm open-minded to the occult.

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:24.710
I'm Nagumo Souichirou.

00:13:24.710 --> 00:13:26.090
Dance Dark.

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:31.540
Sounds like a cop drama.

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:33.650
That's so cool.

00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:36.000
So you actually had a job, then!

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.710
Afterward, I thought I'd try and see 
if Dance had a physical presence,

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:47.340
but, apparently, he refuses 
to let a man ride him.

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:49.430
I hurt my back thanks to that.

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:51.580
Then, while I was laid out for a week

00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:54.570
I remembered all of my pent-up 
dissatisfaction with the force,

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:55.520
so I quit.

00:13:57.250 --> 00:14:00.310
By the way, it's been bothering me a little,

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:07.740
but did you think I got this old 
without ever having a job?

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:11.400
I'm sorry.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:14.900
It was the same dream again.

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:18.700
In the dream, I could look out 
over the entire planet.

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:20.920
I was high up in the distant sky.

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:22.950
Nice view.

00:14:22.950 --> 00:14:27.590
I've wondered this before, but 
am I the only who has this dream?

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:31.220
Anyone could come here 
if Anima or I invited them.

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:32.810
Hmm.

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:40.970
Hey, Shimaki-kun.

00:14:40.970 --> 00:14:43.280
What should we talk about today?

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:47.460
Let's talk about food.

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:49.360
What do you like, Shimaki-kun?

00:14:49.810 --> 00:14:52.200
Lately, I've been into Chinese.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:53.610
That's nice.

00:14:53.610 --> 00:14:55.210
You know, the way I see it,

00:14:55.210 --> 00:14:58.420
food may be regional, 
but it's not bound by borders.

00:14:58.420 --> 00:15:01.420
I doesn't matter what nation it's from, 
good food is good food.

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:04.170
What kind of food do you like, Animus?

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:07.090
Japanese food. I really like soba.

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:09.700
Hmm. You can use chopsticks?

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:12.350
I'm from Japan, you know?

00:15:12.350 --> 00:15:15.950
Well, animus is a psychology term.

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:17.140
Guess it wasn't your real name.

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:19.810
No, Animus is my real name.

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:22.870
It's not that uncommon a name in my era.

00:15:23.550 --> 00:15:24.620
In your era?

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:29.490
Morning, Hyou-kun.

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:31.590
Morning, Kuh.

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:33.660
What did you talk about?

00:15:34.220 --> 00:15:37.620
About food, I think.

00:15:38.010 --> 00:15:41.940
Either way, I wonder why 
Animus wants to talk to me.

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:45.920
That's because you're the one 
most similar to the mage.

00:15:48.620 --> 00:15:50.800
Huh? A time machine?

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:53.510
Yeah. Do you think it's possible?

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:58.650
Time slows down as you 
approach the speed of light,

00:15:59.210 --> 00:16:03.060
so if you wandered around in a sublight 
spaceship and returned to Earth,

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:06.760
time on Earth would be ahead 
of time in the spaceship,

00:16:06.760 --> 00:16:08.570
so yeah, you could go to the future.

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:10.780
Earth Time

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:10.780
Ship Time

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:10.780
Earth Time

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:10.780
Ship Time

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:10.780
Though there aren't any sublight spaceships.

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:12.240
What about the past?

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:14.560
Going back through time?

00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:17.620
You'd know more about that 
than me, wouldn't you?

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:18.830
Huh?

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:21.650
Your field is psychology, right?

00:16:21.650 --> 00:16:24.920
Don't you know anyone 
conducting research on ESP?

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:27.050
That's a stereotype.

00:16:27.050 --> 00:16:29.430
If precognition actually existed,

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:32.570
couldn't one say that meant 
information was going back in time?

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:35.470
I'm talking about actually 
knowing the future,

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:37.390
not just making precisely 
calculated predictions.

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:39.070
If that was actually happening,

00:16:39.070 --> 00:16:41.600
then it would prove there was time travel.

00:16:44.740 --> 00:16:48.900
Still, the idea of a time machine 
falls under the occult.

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:52.100
That was a mistake. I couldn't help myself.

00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:52.960
From what?

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:57.680
Pinning my hopes on science 
and imagining the limits of science.

00:16:57.680 --> 00:16:58.780
What do you mean?

00:16:59.420 --> 00:17:03.500
You got your hopes up 
that a time machine might exist

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:06.500
because I said "in my era" 
during your dream, right?

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:09.490
Hey.

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:12.220
Can't you do anything about that outfit?

00:17:12.220 --> 00:17:14.550
I can't, and I won't.

00:17:15.210 --> 00:17:16.560
Did you want something?

00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:18.030
Hey, Shimaki-kun.

00:17:18.030 --> 00:17:20.210
Would you join my side?

00:17:20.210 --> 00:17:22.770
Forget about the Princess, 
the Knights, and this planet.

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:24.230
What?

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:26.860
I have a feeling you and I 
can get along well.

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:28.390
Let me guess.

00:17:28.390 --> 00:17:33.360
What did you first try asking for 
with the wish of your Knight's pact?

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:37.320
To obtain the Akashic Records.

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:40.040
You tried to learn everything 
about the universe, right?

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:45.110
You tried to become an 
all-knowing being, didn't you?

00:17:46.260 --> 00:17:48.800
Kuh told me it was impossible, though.

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:50.650
He said if he could do that,

00:17:50.650 --> 00:17:55.260
then he would be something on par 
with or even greater than the mage.

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:59.630
Harboring that desire 
is proof you're like me.

00:17:59.630 --> 00:18:02.260
After all, that is what I desire.

00:18:02.670 --> 00:18:03.940
Join me.

00:18:03.940 --> 00:18:06.980
Let's seize the mysteries 
of the universe together.

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:10.810
Ow.

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:13.520
I found the mage!

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:16.290
He's Animus! I'm certain!

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:17.290
Get him!

00:18:17.290 --> 00:18:19.280
Get away from Shimaki-san!

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:21.370
Yuki-chan! Subaru-chan!

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:24.060
Oh? The little rooster 
and the little turtle.

00:18:24.060 --> 00:18:25.250
Hello.

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:27.580
Shut up! Let's go, Yuki!

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:29.670
Yeah, Subaru-chan!

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:38.300
Hmm, I suppose I should take my leave today.

00:18:38.630 --> 00:18:40.780
You can give me your answer later.

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:41.760
Bye.

00:18:43.220 --> 00:18:45.430
W-Wait! Mage!

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:47.350
I have a message from our master!

00:18:47.900 --> 00:18:50.310
He said, "We are human."

00:19:02.440 --> 00:19:05.200
He'll probably summon you again tonight.

00:19:06.860 --> 00:19:09.230
Will you side with Animus?

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:13.630
I thought the destruction of Earth 
was his actual goal.

00:19:13.910 --> 00:19:15.960
But that's not the case.

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:17.590
His goal lies beyond that.

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:20.460
Do you want to know everything 
about the universe?

00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:22.050
Yeah, I do.

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:23.890
I want to know everything.

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:25.260
<b>Principles of Theosophy</b>

00:19:28.260 --> 00:19:31.230
Well, it's exactly what you suspect.

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:33.190
I'm from the future.

00:19:33.710 --> 00:19:37.990
I am the advanced wave originating 
from the future and collapsing space-time

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:41.490
as I travel back to the point 
of origin where all converges.

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:44.800
I am the god of destruction 
born to counterbalance

00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:47.760
the supernatural being known 
as the god who created this universe.

00:19:47.760 --> 00:19:49.290
That's who I am.

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:51.920
That's an awfully grand tale.

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:57.240
Even though I possess the power of a god, 
I was first born in a human vessel.

00:19:57.240 --> 00:19:59.680
That's why I too have a desire.

00:19:59.680 --> 00:20:00.380
A desire—

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:02.340
To know everything.

00:20:02.610 --> 00:20:03.760
Yes.

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:07.390
And I will fulfill my function 
in pursuit of that carnal desire.

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:12.320
I want to see the convergence point 
where everything began with my own eyes.

00:20:12.320 --> 00:20:13.810
Let's go observe it together.

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:19.030
Why would a god reach out 
to an ordinary human like me?

00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:24.870
All of the Knights are people with 
the potential to become my equals.

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:27.270
None of you are ordinary humans.

00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:30.140
Let's be friends, Shimaki-kun.

00:20:30.140 --> 00:20:34.210
Why don't we share in the joy 
of learning everything?

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:40.260
Looks like I can use it, even here.

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:41.460
Use what?

00:20:41.460 --> 00:20:46.300
I'll show you what I wished for 
after asking to know everything.

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:47.130
It was

00:20:47.130 --> 00:20:49.370
a special upgrade to my Holding Field—

00:20:49.370 --> 00:20:51.930
Creation Field: Kybele!

00:20:54.980 --> 00:20:56.390
What?

00:20:56.390 --> 00:20:58.190
A Knight creating golems?!

00:20:58.190 --> 00:21:00.230
Ahh, what an idea!

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:01.940
Wonderful, Shimaki-kun!

00:21:02.210 --> 00:21:05.240
Not a single knight has ever 
thought of this before!

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:11.230
My goal is to use the knowledge of the 
Akashic Records to make all humanity happy.

00:21:11.230 --> 00:21:15.330
So I will crush your tiny ambition.

00:21:15.330 --> 00:21:19.110
Please die here for humanity's sake, god.

00:21:24.210 --> 00:21:25.710
Chaos Field:

00:21:25.710 --> 00:21:26.740
Pandora!

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:33.810
Wha?! You're!

00:21:33.810 --> 00:21:35.460
Let me introduce you.

00:21:35.460 --> 00:21:38.870
He is both the Owl Knight and my Knight,

00:21:38.870 --> 00:21:40.910
Akane Taiyou-kun.

00:21:40.910 --> 00:21:42.030
Don't touch me.

00:21:42.510 --> 00:21:45.700
All this god of destruction 
and happiness of mankind crap...

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:47.410
You two aren't normal.

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:48.490
You're monsters.

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:51.450
Looks like he's at that rebellious age.

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:54.470
What's the meaning of this, 
Akane-kun? You...

00:21:54.470 --> 00:21:56.640
What a shame, Shimaki-kun.

00:21:56.640 --> 00:21:59.680
Well, let's call it a day for now.

00:21:59.680 --> 00:22:00.670
See you later.

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:03.210
Animus! Akane-kun! Wait!

00:22:05.900 --> 00:22:06.870
Morning.

00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:08.240
Morning.

00:22:09.210 --> 00:22:11.260
Did you side with Animus?

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:13.990
I couldn't. Although...

00:22:13.990 --> 00:22:15.010
Although?

00:22:15.880 --> 00:22:17.760
No, I'll leave it be for now.

00:22:17.760 --> 00:22:21.460
The flow of time is a great thing. 
Powerful enough to create gods.

00:22:21.460 --> 00:22:24.220
There's no way of telling 
how fate will play out.

00:22:24.220 --> 00:22:26.990
I don't understand a thing you're saying.

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:29.070
You two aren't normal.

00:22:29.070 --> 00:22:30.200
You're monsters.

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:32.140
Monsters?

00:22:32.140 --> 00:22:34.160
Am I a monster, too?

00:22:34.520 --> 00:22:36.370
No, maybe that's a good thing.

00:22:38.330 --> 00:22:41.670
My role is to be a god-slaying monster.

00:22:41.670 --> 00:22:44.790
An agent of peace that devours 
the guts of an evil god.

00:22:45.440 --> 00:22:50.300
Why not aim to become a monster 
that fights for justice?

00:22:57.040 --> 00:23:05.190
<i>Looking back to those times, 
I always thought</i>

00:23:05.190 --> 00:23:09.750
<i>It was hard to live life true to myself.</i>

00:23:10.410 --> 00:23:13.480
<i>I recall those times.</i>

00:23:13.480 --> 00:23:17.050
<i>I wanted to forget, 
but now it's different.</i>

00:23:17.050 --> 00:23:22.730
<i>Back then we stared at that same sky.</i>

00:23:23.910 --> 00:23:29.460
<i>I'll never forget you, 
or our endless dreams</i>

00:23:29.460 --> 00:23:35.970
<i>As we gazed at that sky 
after fate brought us together</i>

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:41.420
<i>I dream of us together, 
of those days I remember</i>

00:23:41.420 --> 00:23:43.690
<i>But dreams end and I wake up</i>

00:23:43.690 --> 00:23:48.210
<i>Seeking the future</i>

00:23:49.120 --> 00:23:54.260
<i>I reach for the light,</i>

00:23:55.180 --> 00:24:00.680
<i>Always thinking of you in</i>

00:24:04.300 --> 00:24:13.580
<i>every little thing</i>

00:24:22.440 --> 00:24:26.940
<b>Next Episode:
Akitani Inatika</b>
